aPX(a,b){return"1. As an owner of the organisation open github.com/"+a+"/settings.\n2. At the bottom under \u201cDanger Zone\u201d click \u201cTransfer\u201d, enter "+b+" as new owner and confirm.\n3. A personal account has to accept the transfer by e-mail; for an organisation the person transferring needs the right to create repositories there, otherwise the customer invites you first.\n4. Afterwards check the deploy credentials (secrets) in the new repository; the deploy workflow keeps using the customer portal's public template."},
aPV(a,b){return"1. Open github.com/"+a+"/settings/access.\n2. \u201cAdd people\u201d, enter "+b+", choose the role \u201cAdmin\u201d and invite.\n3. The customer accepts the invitation by e-mail or at github.com/notifications.\n4. If the customer wants to own the repository, it can be transferred afterwards (see \u201cTransfer repository\u201d)."},
